# Set the default behavior, in case people don't have core.autocrlf set.
* text=auto

# LF in the working tree, not just in the repository.
#
# Git has always stored these as LF; the `eol=crlf` this replaced only decided what landed on disk
# after a checkout, and it dated from the repo being Windows-first. Every build tool here writes LF,
# so on a Linux checkout the two disagreed on every generated file and git narrated the conversion
# once per file on every `git add`. Nothing at runtime cares - NW.js and every JS engine accept both -
# so the only thing the mismatch produced was noise.
*.js text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# Denote all files that are truly binary and should not be modified.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
